WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.793
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.093 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:14.497
Unit eighteen: Weekend Fun. Today you will talk about different things you do at the weekend.

4
00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:17.286
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:21.373
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:23.044
Weekend.

7
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.200
Weekend means Saturday and Sunday.

8
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:28.932
I visit my grandparents at the weekend.

9
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:31.786
Your turn. Say: Weekend.

10
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:35.542
Weekend.

11
00:00:36.283 --> 00:00:37.226
Relax.

12
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:40.669
Relax means to rest and feel calm.

13
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:43.747
On Sunday mornings, I relax at home.

14
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.118
Your turn. Say: Relax.

15
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:50.991
Relax.

16
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.670
Hang out.

17
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.368
Hang out means to spend free time with friends.

18
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:58.762
We hang out at the riverside.

19
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.689
Your turn. Say: Hang out.

20
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:05.395
Hang out.

21
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:06.989
Movie.

22
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:09.368
Movie means a film.

23
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:11.681
We watched a funny movie.

24
00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:14.924
Your turn. Say: Movie.

25
00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:18.884
Movie.

26
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.883
Outdoors.

27
00:01:21.883 --> 00:01:24.963
Outdoors means outside, not in a building.

28
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.642
We play outdoors when it's cool.

29
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.728
Your turn. Say: Outdoors.

30
00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.498
Outdoors.

31
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.193
Adventure.

32
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:40.205
Adventure means an exciting, unusual experience.

33
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:43.141
Hiking up Phnom Kulen was an adventure.

34
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.565
Your turn. Say: Adventure.

35
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.471
Adventure.

36
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:52.078
Free time.

37
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:56.000
Free time means time when you don't have to work or study.

38
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:58.442
What do you do in your free time?

39
00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.470
Your turn. Say: Free time.

40
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:05.346
Free time.

41
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:07.050
Enjoy.

42
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.096
Enjoy means to like doing something.

43
00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:13.217
I enjoy every moment with my family.

44
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:16.190
Your turn. Say: Enjoy.

45
00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.174
Enjoy.

46
00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:24.281
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:27.058
Visal, what do you do at the weekend?

48
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:33.624
It changes! Sometimes we watch a movie, and sometimes we go outdoors.

49
00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:36.298
Where do you go outdoors?

50
00:02:37.383 --> 00:02:42.343
Sometimes we cycle to Koh Dach, and sometimes we play football.

51
00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.124
Do you ever just relax?

52
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:51.481
Yes! On Sunday evening, I relax and get ready for school.

53
00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:54.099
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.099
Grammar focus: Sometimes and sometimes.

55
00:02:58.399 --> 00:02:59.493
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:00.183 --> 00:03:04.006
Sometimes we watch a movie, and sometimes we go outdoors.

57
00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.497
Sometimes I read, and sometimes I draw.

58
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:11.985
Sometimes she cooks, and sometimes she sings karaoke.

59
00:03:12.933 --> 00:03:16.489
Use this pattern to show that you do different things at different times.

60
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:22.607
Be careful! Don't say: Sometimes we watch a movie, sometimes go outdoors.

61
00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:29.329
Say: Sometimes we watch a movie, and sometimes we go outdoors.

62
00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:32.453
Use 'and' and repeat the subject in the second part.

63
00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.221
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.174
My Weekends.

65
00:03:38.474 --> 00:03:41.890
On the weekend, I love to relax and hang out with friends.

66
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.769
Sometimes we watch a movie, and sometimes we go outdoors for an adventure.

67
00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:51.833
Last month, we cycled to Koh Dach and ate fresh mangoes.

68
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:56.203
On Sunday, I sometimes help my mother at the market.

69
00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.430
Free time is precious, so I try to enjoy every moment.

70
00:04:01.533 --> 00:04:05.349
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:09.030
Sometimes I read, blank sometimes I draw.

72
00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.951
A, and. B, but. C, so.

73
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.058
The answer is A: and.

74
00:04:18.217 --> 00:04:20.553
To spend free time with friends is to blank.

75
00:04:20.853 --> 00:04:24.588
A, hang out. B, relax. C, enjoy.

76
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.168
The answer is A: hang out.

77
00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:34.129
An exciting, unusual experience is an blank.

78
00:04:34.429 --> 00:04:38.349
A, adventure. B, outdoors. C, weekend.

79
00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.760
The answer is A: adventure.

80
00:04:44.967 --> 00:04:47.863
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:48.717 --> 00:04:50.902
What do you usually do for fun on the weekend?

82
00:04:59.717 --> 00:05:01.321
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:01.621 --> 00:05:08.323
Sometimes I hang out with my friends at the park, and sometimes I watch a movie at home with my family.

84
00:05:08.623 --> 00:05:10.356
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.667
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and sometimes and sometimes.

86
00:05:15.967 --> 00:05:20.895
Today's value is balance. Enjoy screens a little, then play and read too.

87
00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:23.987
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:24.287 --> 00:05:26.881
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

